<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105580" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροχαῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόχος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>running, spinning,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανία</span> (<i>spools</i>) <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.288
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροχαῖος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πούς</span>), ὁ, a
			<i>trochee</i> or <i>foot consisting of a long and a short
				syllable</i> (also called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορεῖος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				400b
			</span></i>, etc.; used in quick time, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1408b36
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Po.</u>
				1452b24
			</span></i>, and 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροχερός</span>
			 :—hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Music, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ σαλπικταὶ τροχαῖόν
				τι συμβοήσαντες</span> playing <i>a brisk march,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				56.22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. νόμος</span> a tune <i>in
				trochaic time,</i> invented by Terpander, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1132d
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.65
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>tribrach</i> (^ ^ ^), <i><span class="en">
				Quint.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				9.4.82
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. σημαντὸς ὁ ἐξ ὀκτασήμου θέσεως καὶ
				τετ ρασήμου ἄρσεως</span> (&lt;*&gt; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">¯</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.Quint.
				1.16
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἀπὸ ἰάμβου</span> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">¯̆</span>|<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">¯̆</span>) ibid. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροχαῖα: μέσα ἐν κύβοις, ἢ ὁδός, ὡς
				Ῥίνθων</span> (<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				26
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόχια</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροχιά</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
